Z||000000||newfie||11-24-2001||03:40 PM||||This is not a supercharger Vs. turbo post just a few supercharger Q's.  First off has anyone had any experience with the kit at RSM racing.  <A HREF="http://www.rsmracing.com," TARGET=_blank>www.rsmracing.com,</A>  Is there any other kits out there?  I know someone on this board was planning on making a kit using an Eaton.  I don't see how this is possible using the stock fiero intake and the outlet on the eaton.  Also I was looking at some Vortech SC's and they look like belt driven turbo's, Is this all it is?? Is there anyway to adjust the amount of boost a SC uses without changing the pulley?  A boost controller?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||lowCG||11-26-2001||08:47 PM||||Pulley size controls the boost,it would be neat to see an Eaton on top of a V6,in one of our cars.Probably would require a manifold from another 60degree motor,with an adaptor...||||reg||1
Z||000002||TRiAD||11-26-2001||10:07 PM||||That was me...and it would use a custom intake manifold...due to other problems with the donor and my current occupational impairment (I'm laid-off) the project is postponed. <P>If the job market clears quickly (doubtful) the car will immediately be back on the road and the project will be underway. <P>Other than that...anything you add should provide decent gains, the way it goes about it (lag or no, low or high end, etc) should be the only major differences...oh, and reliability. <P>Good luck!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||11-27-2001||08:35 AM||||you can put an eaton in the same location as the A/C condenser.. just like the RSM system (rsm sells vortech (a-trim) along with rotrex for their systems) you don't have to have a roots type on top of the engine.. there are thousands of miatas running around with an M45 2' away fron the intake..just plumed in like a centrifugal. many military vehicles run roots type  suspended from the frame and plumed into the intake system. ||||reg||1
